    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9036" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">collecta</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conl-</span></b> ), ae, f. (orig.
		adj., sc. pecunia) [colligo]. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A contribution in money</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">a convivā exigere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 2, 57, 233</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 6, 66</span></i>
			Müll.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A meeting</i>, <i>assemblage</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">virginum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 108</span></i>
			, n. 19.</div>
